# ===========================================================================
# ANCHORING RULE - read this before adding a pattern.
#
# A pattern with no leading slash matches at EVERY depth. `data/` does not mean
# "the data directory at the repo root", it means "any directory called data,
# anywhere". That silently excluded three install-critical files:
#
#   addons/custom_pdp_core/data/pdp.field.classification.csv   (724-row contract 01 map)
#   addons/custom_pdp_masking/data/pdp_masking_rule_data.xml
#   addons/custom_ppob/data/ir_sequence_data.xml
#
# All three are declared in their manifests, so a fresh clone could not install
# those modules - while every local check passed, because the files existed in
# the working tree. `git status` shows nothing. Tests pass. It only surfaces on
# a clean clone.
#
# So: if a pattern names a directory that exists at the ROOT and is runtime
# state, ANCHOR IT with a leading slash. Leave a pattern unanchored only when
# the name is an artefact everywhere it appears (node_modules, __pycache__,
# .ruff_cache).
#
# Escape hatch, if a needed file is ever caught anyway:
#   git add -f <path>          # tracks it despite the pattern
#   git check-ignore -v --no-index <path>   # shows which line matched
# `git add -f` fixes one file; it does NOT fix the pattern, so the next file at
# that path is dropped again. Fix the pattern.
#
# `make verify` fails if an ignored file appears under a source root.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. `.env` holds generated dev credentials; `.env.example` (tracked)
# holds only the literal string `changeme`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.bak-*
.age-key.txt
*.agekey

# Private key material, at any depth - deliberately unanchored, and deliberately
# fail-safe: a file called *.key or *.pem is presumed private.
*.pem
*.key
# ...but PUBLIC keys and certificates must ship. The login-gateway publishes a
# JWKS and its verifiers need the public half (contract 02), so these come back.
!**/*.pub
!**/*.pub.pem
!**/*public*.pem
!**/*.crt
!**/*.pub.key

# Unanchored on purpose: a directory called `secrets` should be ignored wherever
# it appears. Nothing that must ship belongs in one. Use `git add -f` for a
# README describing the layout.
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state - bind-mounted or generated at the repo ROOT. Never tracked.
# ANCHORED: `data/`, `backups/` and `logs/` unanchored swallowed addon seed
# data, dbt seeds and any nested logs/ a service ships.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/backups/
/logs/
*.log

# Machine-local Postgres override, loaded by `include_if_exists` at the end of
# postgres/postgresql.conf.
/postgres/conf.d/local.conf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language / tooling artefacts.
# Unanchored where the directory name is an artefact at any depth; anchored
# where a source tree could legitimately use the name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
# ANCHORED: a dbt project can legitimately have models/.../build/.
/build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
coverage/
.coverage

# dbt (Data Warehouse agent) - already path-anchored.
analytics/dbt/target/
analytics/dbt/logs/
analytics/dbt/dbt_packages/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~
